      "text": "Sarvottam Cables is a manufacturer of power cables, wires and conductors.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E1"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q1 FY27 (quarter ended 30 June 2026) consolidated revenue from operations was ₹1,248 crore, up 18.0% year-on-year.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E1"}, {"id": "S3:E3"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q1 FY27 consolidated profit after tax was ₹82 crore, up 5.9% year-on-year.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E6"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q1 FY27 consolidated EBITDA margin was 11.2%, down 170 basis points from 12.9% a year earlier.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E5"}]
    }
  ],
  "Bull case": [
    {
      "text": "Order book stood at ₹3,900 crore as of 30 June 2026, up from ₹3,150 crore a year earlier.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E7"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The company says the Bharuch plant, adding about 30% to cable capacity, is on track for Q3 FY27 commercial production; management maintained FY27 revenue growth guidance of 15–17%.",
      "citations": ["S3", "S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E9"}, {"id": "S2:E1"}]
    }
  ],
  "Bear case": [
    {
      "text": "Q1 FY27 EBITDA margin fell 170 bps to 11.2%; the MD attributed this mostly to copper prices, noting two-thirds of contracts have price-variation clauses that reset with a one-to-two-quarter lag.",
      "citations": ["S3", "S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E5"}, {"id": "S2:E3"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The CFO stated receivable days rose from 78 to 96 over the last year, mainly due to two large state utility customers; no defaults have been reported.",
      "citations": ["S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S2:E5"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The company received a CGST demand of ₹46.3 crore including interest and penalty for ITC claimed in FY2020-21 and FY2021-22; it states it intends to file an appeal before the appropriate authority.",
